      "area": "concurrency",
      "premise": "At head, every call to addrConn.resetTransportAndUnlock (clientconn.go connect and updateAddrs) holds ac.mu, and every return path of resetTransportAndUnlock releases ac.mu exactly once before doing blocking work, so no path double-unlocks or leaks the lock.",
      "evidence": [
        {"coordinate": "clientconn.go:922", "text": "ac.resetTransportAndUnlock()"},
        {"coordinate": "clientconn.go:996", "text": "go ac.resetTransportAndUnlock()"},
        {"coordinate": "clientconn.go:1234", "text": "func (ac *addrConn) resetTransportAndUnlock() {"}
